[2026-05-19T21:46:27.686Z] [INFO]   ✅ Found pull request #154: "Better search support and diagnostics UI/UX improvements"
[2026-05-19T21:46:28.036Z] [STDOUT] ## Summary

Resolves #153.

This PR completes the search/diagnostics/UI overhaul and addresses the latest PR review feedback on the refreshed screenshots:

- SVO formalization now renders every search prompt as `(@USER OP:<verb> <object>)`, then shows the resolved Wikidata id when available, for example `(@USER OP:search Q89)`.
- Diagnostics mode shows formalization, source counts, tool inputs/outputs, and trace evidence with consistent spacing.
- DuckDuckGo search is fixed, Internet Archive search is added, and fused search results dedupe matching Wikipedia/Wikidata entities into one localized result with an `Other sources:` line.
- The top menu now has the Source code link, lab diagnostics emoji, disabled empty-chat New conversation state, and priority-based overflow where Bug reporting, Diagnostics, and Demo remain visible longest.
- Desktop and mobile menus expose the full action list; the desktop sidebar can collapse without constraining the chat/composer.
- The case study in `docs/case-studies/issue-153/` now includes the issue data, original screenshots, root-cause analysis, requirement mapping, and the post-review layout fix notes.

## Latest Review Follow-Up

The 2026-05-19 review comment called out three broken screenshots. This update fixes and re-validates each one:

| Feedback | Fix |
| --- | --- |
| `desktop-1440-fresh.png` did not fit; buttons needed to move into the menu | Desktop topbar switches to icon-only labels by 1500px, hides status-only items by 1100px, and keeps the desktop sidebar Menu visible as the full action fallback. |
| `03-sidebar-collapsed.png` showed the input/composer in the wrong layout | `.workspace.sidebar-collapsed` now uses a single full-width grid column, and the e2e test asserts `.chat-panel` and `.composer` span the viewport. |
| `diagnostics-formalization.png` had uneven alignment and padding | Diagnostics details, formalization blocks, payloads, tool sections, and source-count rows now share consistent spacing and borders. |

## Screenshots

| View | Screenshot |
| --- | --- |
| Desktop 1440 topbar, no clipped actions | ![Desktop 1440](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-153-9ae03e768324/docs/screenshots/issue-153/desktop-1440-fresh.png?raw=true) |
| Diagnostics formalization and tool output spacing | ![Diagnostics formalization](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-153-9ae03e768324/docs/screenshots/issue-153/diagnostics-formalization.png?raw=true) |
| Desktop sidebar collapsed, chat/composer full width | ![Sidebar collapsed](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-153-9ae03e768324/docs/screenshots/issue-153/03-sidebar-collapsed.png?raw=true) |
| Mobile 375 priority topbar | ![Mobile prioritized](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-153-9ae03e768324/docs/screenshots/issue-153/mobile-375-prioritized.png?raw=true) |
| Mobile 375 drawer with full action list | ![Mobile drawer](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-153-9ae03e768324/docs/screenshots/issue-153/mobile-375-drawer.png?raw=true) |

## Priority Mapping

| Priority | Topbar behavior |
| --- | --- |
| 1 | Bug reporting remains visible the longest. |
| 2 | Diagnostics remains visible with Bug reporting on mobile. |
| 3 | Demo mode remains visible with priorities 1-2 on mobile. |
| 4 | Chat/Agent moves to the Menu before priorities 1-3. |
| 5 | Source code moves to the Menu before priorities 1-4. |
| 6 | Export/import memory move to the Menu first among action buttons. |
| 7 | Status-only items hide before action buttons. |

## Validation

- [x] `npm --prefix tests/e2e run test:local -- --workers=1` — 128 passed.
- [x] `npm --prefix tests/e2e run test:local -- --grep "Issue #153|demo mode starts automatically|memory export/import|Issue #27: agent mode"` — 27 passed.
- [x] `npm --prefix tests/e2e run test:local -- --grep "toolbar labels switch|demo mode starts automatically|Issue #153"` — 11 passed.
- [x] `npm --prefix tests/e2e run check:i18n` — 4 locales, 126 keys.
- [x] `git diff --check` — passed on the latest commit.
- [x] `rust-script scripts/check-file-size.rs` — passed on the latest commit; warnings are existing near-limit Rust files.
- [x] `cargo fmt --all -- --check` — passed before the final docs-only commit.
- [x] `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features` — passed before the final docs-only commit; no Rust/source changes afterward.
- [x] `cargo test --all-features --verbose` — passed before the final docs-only commit; no Rust/source changes afterward.

## Reproducing The Main Fixes

1. Send `Search the web for Apple` with diagnostics enabled. The trace shows `(@USER OP:search ?Apple)`, then `(@USER OP:search Q89)` after Wikidata resolution.
2. Inspect the rendered search answer. Wikipedia and Wikidata entries for the same entity collapse into one result with `Other sources:`.
3. Resize the app at 1440 / 1320 / 1180 / 1040 / 980 / 375px. Visible topbar actions stay within the viewport, and the Menu exposes hidden actions.
4. Collapse the desktop sidebar. The chat panel and composer remain full-width.
5. Open diagnostics. Formalization and tool details use uniform spacing and aligned payload blocks.

